Yet another Stupid First Near-Ascension Death

Playing a wizard for only the second time in over six months, I managed to
get my first-ever near ascension. (I got used to getting killed by
minotaurs, in the Valley of the Dead, or by Master Kaen.) Too bad I made a
bunch of stupid mistakes along the way.

Apsic started lucky. Her first two spellbooks were Force Bolt and Healing,
and she also started with a =oTeleport and b/oCharging. She was able to
make it through the mines only gaining one level, so protection was
obtained cheaply. The first Tengu she killed provided poly control, so a
lot of extra wandering was saved by putting the ring on until a leprechaun
hall made it superfluous.

Soko gave up reflection. A polytrap on level 12 gave her a jabberwock and
later a green dragon. The first blue dragon she killed dropped scales. The
Dark One was shockingly easy when I went after him at lv 15 with a -21AC;
I thought the quest would be doable, but after so many times being pounded
by Master Kaen I was shocked.

There was no Ludios, but I found a coaligned altar on level 22 (two levels
above Medusa, whose level dropped straight into the castle), and made that
my base; it took a few trips of going up to my old stash at Sokoban (and
some last goodies from Minetown obtained with my jabberwock's help) to
establish myself there. In the castle courtyard, I got five nurses from a
c/oGeno, and boosted my HP from 124 to 230. I used the /oW for GDSM (+0),
a cornuthaum (+3), and two magic markers, and wrote myself a few nice
spellbooks and scrolls of enchant armor. Too bad I didn't write remove
curse....

That being the second one, I made some serious tactical errors, enough
that I was lucky to survive as long as I did. First, I'd boosted my
quarterstaff skill to Expert before doing so with dagger; I had to wait
until I was lv 18 in order to do so. When the Castle throne offered me the
chance to geno, I chose Demi-Liches instead of Arch-L. I didn't think to
find the vibrating square before taking the Amulet, so I had to kill
Rodney ten times on the way down, and on one occasion killed a pet when my
Finger of Death exceeded the range visible by my magic lamp. I also
Fingered the HP of Moloch (along with Double Trouble Rodney) before
entering the temple, so Thoth was a little annoyed ("You murderer!"). But
then there was the real stupidity....

While wielding a cockatrice corpse to rid myself of a couple pesky master
liches and their friends, my BoH got cursed. This was doubly annoying
since it had taken me until the second fake tower level to find one, and
until then I'd been satisfied with a sack. Overrelying on Magicbane, I'd
forgotten to keep some holy water and other essentials outside the BoH.
Gone away went four b!oWater and two of three magic markers leaving me
with one (1:8) unable to write remove curse.  And I still don't know how
I lost Magicbane entirely many hours later when I was still trying
to get out of Gehennom. (Can Rodney steal it? I thought he only took the
Amulet and invocation artifacts.) I tried going back down a few levels,
then finally abandoned the search after realizing what a treadmill I'd be
on if I got teleported down again during the climb back.

While in Gehennom, magic mapping, cone of cold, fireball, and magic
missile all faded on me. I mostly made it back up (climbing the stairs at
least 40 times for 22 levels of dungeon) through liberal use of charm
monster (which got me a couple pet purple worms who just loved to swallow
L) when a L or the dungeon created a new ring of monsters around me. Also
of note: peaceful and tame umber hulks rock in Gehennom. :)

Once finally up at the castle, I found another BoH on a generated monster
(lucky da!), and the run to level 1 was uneventful except for a critical
failure of intelligence. When stopping at my cache to re-study the spells
that had faded in Gehennom, I didn't take along the books for the spells
that would likely run out on the Planes, including Finger of Death. I also
forgot my crystal ball.

Plane of Earth was mostly uneventful; I found the portal with a minimum of
hassle, mostly by watching warned creatures disappear when I got near the
right cavern. Air, on the other hand was a bother. I'd brought along four
b!oLevitation, but somehow no backup source. My ascension kit was very
incomplete as it turned out. I put on the AoY to find the portal, but
never got any closer than "very warm", even while whistling pets
constantly in the hopes that one would land on it. I had to kill Rodney a
few more times, and at one point the huge uh-oh set in: I was straining to
recall FoD.

Finally I was killed by a pissy archon who summoned three hordes with a
total of four master mind flayers. Both Charm Monster and Finger of Death
were gone, my wand of death ran out, and an uncursed unicorn horn could
not keep up with the brainsucker sandwich; I went down fighting until I
had less in my head than Rocky Balboa. Died of Brainlessness (seems
appropriate) at 25 with a max of 349hp. I did get top score, naturally:
2,921,815 points was more than three times my previous best. But Oh,
it would have been great to get through just three more levels. ;) My
first endgame... now I feel a second isn't altogether far away.

Notable kills: Rodney 35 times, 12 arch-liches, 16 master liches, 2
archons. (4426 creatures vanquished)

Genocided 1 type of monster (demi-liches) No PolyObj, no PolySelf. Used 4
wishes, none for artifacts. Reverse-genoed nurses twice. (Why doesn't this
count toward genocide conduct? I'd call it an oversight.)



